    "title": "pandas.Timedelta.to_numpy — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timedelta.to_numpy#\n\n- \nTimedelta.to_numpy(*dtype=None* ,*copy=False* )#\n- Convert the Timedelta to a NumPy timedelta64. This is an alias method for Timedelta.to_timedelta64(). \n  - Parameters:\n    - **dtype** NoneType\n    - It is available here only for compatibility. Its value will not affect the return value.\n    - **copy** bool, default False\n    - It is available here only for compatibility. Its value will not affect the return value.\n  - Returns:\n    - numpy.timedelta64\n See also \n  - `Series.to_numpy`\n  - Similar method for Series.\n Examples >>> td = pd.Timedelta('3D') >>> td Timedelta('3 days 00:00:00') >>> td.to_numpy() np.timedelta64(259200000000,'us')",
    "markdown_length": 679,
